# Installation Guide
## Modules
To install the project's required dependencies, paste the following command in the terminal:
> npm install express ejs sqlite3 express-session socket.io dotenv
This should create package.json and package-lock.json files. Edit the package.json file to include the corret name, description, main, author, and license.
It should look something like this:
> {
>    "name": "your_project_name",
>    "description": "your_description",
>    "main": "app.js",
>    "author": "your_name",
>    "license": "your_license" ,
>    "dependencies": {
>        "dotenv": "^17.2.3",
>       "ejs": "^3.1.10",
>       "express": "^5.2.1",
>        "express-session": "^1.18.2",
>        "socket.io": "^4.8.1",
>       "sqlite3": "^5.1.7"
>    }
> }

## Templates
### Environment Variables
Copy the .env_template file. Rename it to .env. Configure your port, session secret, formbar API key and redirect path, and your data directories.

### gitignore
Copy the .gitignore_template file. Rename it to .gitignore. Configure your data directories, and add any additional files you'd like to ignore.